      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "5caeb5635183ec6d45eb0849",
      "mergedPostDetails": "So there is a huge bug in how VRC handles people being in two different versions of a world. If objectSync is added to an existing object and you try to join the world when the instance was made in the old version and still has people in it (a version without ObjectSync on that Object), the client just freezes on join.\n\nThis makes updating the world a nightmare because nothing is done to make sure everyone is on the same version AND because they are not on the same version late joiners freeze. The idea that the instances will slowly die out is unacceptable.\n\nEither everyone needs to be forced to the same version, or the client needs to handle this gracefully.\n\nMaybe of note: In my case Sync physics, and collision transfer were both off on the ObjectSync component.\n\nLog: https://drive.google.com/open?id=18eibeQWekoc_2e6XQVsCSbhBQUmodp7y",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Client Freezes when ObjectSync is added to an Object and players are in different versions of the world",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "5a0e33176a9a2f24c5c1ab21",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
    },
